  "linux_64_meta_yaml": {
    "about": {
      "description": "GM2Calc calculates the new physics contributions to the anomalous magnetic\nmoment of the muon a_mu = (g-2)/2 in the real MSSM and in the Two-Higgs\nDoublet Model (THDM) at the 1- and leading 2-loop level.  An estimate of\nthe theory uncertainty associated with the calculation can also be\nprovided.  GM2Calc can be run from the command line reading SLHA, GM2Calc-\nspecific or THDM input, and provides C, C++, Mathematica and Python\ninterfaces to its library.\n\nReferences:\n  * Eur.Phys.J. C76 (2016) no.2, 62 [arXiv:1510.08071]\n  * Eur.Phys.J. C82 (2022) no.3, 229 [arXiv:2110.13238]\n\nThe `gm2calc-python` package differs from the upstream in its use of the\nctypes interface instead of cppyy to allow for compatibility with environments\nthe have ROOT installed, as ROOT's vendored cppyy disallows cppyy to be installed\nin the same environment.",
      "dev_url": "https://github.com/GM2Calc/GM2Calc",
      "doc_url": "https://gm2calc.github.io/",
      "home": "https://gm2calc.hepforge.org/",
      "license": "GPL-3.0-or-later",
      "license_family": "GPL-3.0-or-later",
      "license_file": "COPYING",
      "summary": "Calculates BSM contributions to the anomalous magnetic moment of the muon (g-2)"
    },
    "build": {
      "number": "2",
      "run_exports": {
        "weak": [
          "gm2calc"
        ]
      },
      "script": "build.sh"
    },
