  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"2.3.1\"\n\nrecipe:\n  # Have top level name be unique from any outputs\n  # c.f. https://github.com/conda-forge/conda-forge.github.io/blob/e6aca9676e9045a677249900354a9d43a2cf4caa/docs/maintainer/knowledge_base.mdx?plain=1#L1656\n  name: gm2calc-suite\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/GM2Calc/GM2Calc/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 24a4b0801adb20e253115d715e6f2edd33d44538700a533be606c456486ecabb\n\nbuild:\n  number: 2\n  skip:\n    - win\n\noutputs:\n  - package:\n      name: gm2calc\n    build:\n      script: build.sh\n    requirements:\n      build:\n        - ${{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n        - ${{ compiler(\"cxx\") }}\n        - cmake\n        - ninja\n      host:\n        # Boost and Eigen are header-only dependencies, so they are only needed\n        # to build GM2Calc and do not create a runtime dependency.\n        - libboost-headers\n        # gm2calc v2.3.1 is compatible with Eigen v3 but not v5\n        - eigen-abi-devel >=3.4.0,<5.0.0.0.0a0\n      run_exports:\n        - ${{ pin_subpackage(\"gm2calc\", upper_bound=\"x.x\") }}\n\n    tests:\n      - package_contents:\n          strict: true\n          bin:\n            - gm2calc.x\n          lib:\n            - gm2calc\n          include:\n            - gm2calc/*.h\n            - gm2calc/*.hpp\n          files:\n            - share/pkgconfig/gm2calc.pc\n            - etc/conda/test-files/gm2calc/0/*\n\n      - files:\n          recipe:\n            - example.gm2\n        script:\n          - gm2calc.x --version\n          - gm2calc.x --help\n          - gm2calc.x --gm2calc-input-file=example.gm2\n\n  - package:\n      name: gm2calc-python\n    build:\n      python:\n        version_independent: true\n      script:\n        - mkdir -p \"${SP_DIR}\"\n        - cp \"${RECIPE_DIR}/gm2calc.py\" \"${SP_DIR}/gm2calc.py\"\n        # Add type stubs\n        - cp \"${RECIPE_DIR}/gm2calc.pyi\" \"${SP_DIR}/gm2calc.pyi\"\n\n    requirements:\n      host:\n        - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n      run:\n        - python >=${{ python_min }}\n        # The interface calls libgm2calc's C API through ctypes so only the\n        # gm2calc library itself is needed.\n        - ${{ pin_subpackage(\"gm2calc\", exact=True) }}\n\n    tests:\n      - python:\n          imports:\n            - gm2calc\n          python_version:\n            - ${{ python_min }}.*\n            - \"*\"\n\n      - files:\n          recipe:\n            - test_example_gm2calc.py\n            - test_example_slha.py\n            - test_example_thdm.py\n        script:\n          - python ./test_example_gm2calc.py\n          - python ./test_example_slha.py\n          - python ./test_example_thdm.py\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://gm2calc.hepforge.org\n  repository: https://github.com/GM2Calc/GM2Calc\n  documentation: https://gm2calc.github.io\n  license: GPL-3.0-or-later\n  license_file: COPYING\n  summary: Calculates BSM contributions to the anomalous magnetic moment of the muon (g-2)\n  description: |\n    GM2Calc calculates the new physics contributions to the anomalous magnetic\n    moment of the muon a_mu = (g-2)/2 in the real MSSM and in the Two-Higgs\n    Doublet Model (THDM) at the 1- and leading 2-loop level.  An estimate of\n    the theory uncertainty associated with the calculation can also be\n    provided.  GM2Calc can be run from the command line reading SLHA, GM2Calc-\n    specific or THDM input, and provides C, C++, Mathematica and Python\n    interfaces to its library.\n\n    References:\n      * Eur.Phys.J. C76 (2016) no.2, 62 [arXiv:1510.08071]\n      * Eur.Phys.J. C82 (2022) no.3, 229 [arXiv:2110.13238]\n\n    The `gm2calc-python` package differs from the upstream in its use of the\n    ctypes interface instead of cppyy to allow for compatibility with environments\n    the have ROOT installed, as ROOT's vendored cppyy disallows cppyy to be installed\n    in the same environment.\n\nextra:\n  feedstock-name: gm2calc\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - matthewfeickert\n",
